<title>CANADA: NOVA will not join Methanex buyback.</title>
<headline>NOVA will not join Methanex buyback.</headline>
<dateline>VANCOUVER 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Methanex Corp said Thursday that 25 percent owner NOVA Corp will not participate in Methanex's share buyback.</p>
<p>Methanex earlier announced plans to buy back up to 10 percent of its shares over the next year. Methanex stock was up 0.20 to 11.80 in Toronto.</p>
<p>&quot;NOVA will not participate in the buyback,&quot; Methanex chief executive Pierre Choquette told a conference call.</p>
<p>By not participating, NOVA, a chemicals and natural gas concern, will see its percentage ownership in Methanex grow. It is a &quot;long term shareholder,&quot; Methanex said. Methanex is the world's biggest methanol producer.</p>
<p>((Reuters Vancouver Bureau (604) 664-7314))</p>
</text>
